  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN and an integer KKK.\n\nIn one operation, you may select an integer 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N and increase AiA_iAi​ by 111.\n\nAfter performing all operations, create a bar graph-like shape as follows:\n\n\nFirst, add a rectangle with width 111 and height A1A_1A1​ bounded by x=0,x=1,y=0,y=A1x=0, x=1, y=0, y=A_1x=0,x=1,y=0,y=A1​.\nFor each 2≤i≤N2 \\leq i \\leq N2≤i≤N, append a 1×Ai1\\times A_i1×Ai​ rectangle to the right of the current shape, bounded by the lines x=i−1,x=i,y=0,y=Aix=i-1, x=i, y=0, y=A_ix=i−1,x=i,y=0,y=Ai​.\nIt can be shown that this shape has a contiguous area, and thus its perimeter is well defined.\n\nOutput the minimum number of operations such that the perimeter of this shape is **at most** KKK. Output −1-1−1 if this is impossible no matter what operations are done.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK, the size of the array AAA and the maximum allowed perimeter.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of operations, or −1-1−1 if no set of operations can make the condition hold.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K≤10181 \\le K \\le 10^{18}1≤K≤1018",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n3 10\n2 1 2\n5 2\n1 2 3 4 5\n1 9\n2\n6 35\n7 3 4 2 8 9\n6 31\n9 6 3 6 7 8",
        "output": "1\n-1\n0\n6\n10",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Initially the perimeter is 121212, but after we update A2A_2A2​ by adding 111, the new perimeter is 101010. Thus, one operation is sufficient.\n\nTest Case 2 : It can be proven to be impossible."
